The above brute force approach was correct. But then he
told me to optimize the solution. So what I did is to use the
method similar to the problem - (Find the number of
subarrays whose sum is 0).
I explained to him how the above optimized solution will
work and also wrote the code for the above problem.
int subarraySum(vector<int>& nums, int k) {
int sum=0;
int ans=0;
unordered_map<int,int> u;
u[0]=1;
for(int i=0;i<int(nums.size());i++){
sum=sum+nums[i];
ans=ans+u[sum-k];
u[sum]++;
}
return ans;
}
